  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (pp5-6); Sale of bonds 660,000 is inside printed Total revenues, recorded as debt_proceeds. Rural fire reimbursement 29,815 is printed under other financing sources (outside Total revenues). Beginning/ending governmental cash = fund balances (all assets are cash/CDs, no liabilities); investments (CDs) informational and inside cash. Business-type from proprietary statement (p8), measure net position; totals = operating + nonoperating. Balance sheet from government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1, Total column) because it holds capital assets and debt. The only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (pp9-10), so detail is per fund column of the governmental funds and proprietary funds statements; interest income and interest expense on p8 are nonoperating (outside the printed operating totals). Government-wide business-type cash 267,873/CDs 3,401 vs proprietary statement 267,874/3,400 (rounding between statements; totals agree). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
